A young farmhand at the village kept a chalk tally on a beam in the barn — one mark for each egg the goose laid, one cross for each coin paid at the market. The goose laid 1 golden egg a day for 20 days, and when the eggs were finally carried in their basket to the market they fetched 900 coins in all — the boy stood and stared up at the marks, while Alex sat by the door of the barn, grateful for every bite, listening to the goose ruffle her feathers.

