Beneath a low vine in an old vineyard Renard the fox had been leaping at a heavy cluster of ripe purple grapes for the better part of an hour. He, weak with hunger, had resolved before starting that 7 attempts would be his limit — beyond that, he would call the grapes sour and walk away. So far he had sprung 1 time, paws scrabbling at the leaves, and now he stood panting in the dust to weigh whether the next jump was worth its breath.

