On the first hard morning of winter — a season that would last 67 days in all — Hum the grasshopper came scratching at Tic's burrow, weak with hunger. Inside the burrow, Tic sat beside a hole of 64 acorns and ate 3 acorns each day. The Grasshopper had only 20 acorns in a basket, and ate 3 acorns a day. (No stockpile can drop below zero.)

Question: how many acorns Tic has left at the end of winter?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
I compute leftover for Tic as initial minus days times rate, then clamp to 0 if negative using max.

{"tool_calls":[{"name":"eval","args":{"form":"(let [ant-stock 64 ant-rate 3 gh-stock 20 gh-rate 3 days 67 ant-left (- ant-stock (* ant-rate days)) gh-left (- gh-stock (* gh-rate days))] (max ant-left 0))"}}]}
<|end|>


