It is said that the foolish Dog will trade what is real for what is only an image.

Rex the dog arrived at Emily's back gate with 7 bones stacked carefully in a small basket. Emily eyed the pile and offered a deal: hand over 2 bones of those plain bones, and she would give back the same number of much bigger ones from a sack in the shed. He agreed, with a hungry gleam in his eye. But when Emily returned, only 1 bone dropped from the sack into the basket — fewer than promised, and Emily shrugged as if he ought to be grateful.

Question: how many bones Rex has after the trade?
