A young shepherd had been left alone with the flock far too often, and boredom had taken root.

On the door of the village hall hung a small slate where the reeve marked false alarms with a chalked stroke. The rule was plain: more than 3 marks on the slate and the village no longer turned out. Jess's slate showed 0 marks so far, and the shepherd, his heart sinking, looked at it on the way home each evening.

Write a Clojure expression that computes whether the villagers will come on the next alarm (return the string "yes" or "no").
