Three Bulls had grazed and fought together for so long that no Lion dared trouble them.

Along an old fence-line that the herd had once walked together each evening, 3 bulls now drifted past the rails singly. Every bull had a measured strength of 4, and Roar the lion, at 12, padded the far side with eyes always on the path. One bull at the fence was no contest for him; the herd at full muster, however, mounted a combined strength of 12, which would have flung the lion clean off the rails. The bulls' unease left them wide-eyed with fear, drifting further apart each night. The remaining question was a yes-or-no.

Write a Clojure expression that computes whether Roar can defeat each bull alone (lion-strength > bull-strength) yet would lose against the herd combined (lion-strength < combined-strength).
