Strength shared is strength multiplied — a truth the Lion knew well, and worked patiently to undo. This was at the edge of the woods.

Along an old fence-line that the herd had once walked together each evening, 3 bulls now drifted past the rails singly. Every bull had a measured strength of 4, and Mane the lion, at 10, padded the far side saying very little. One bull at the fence was no contest for her; the herd at full muster, however, mounted a combined strength of 12, which would have flung the lion clean off the rails. The bulls' unease left them shouting until her voice cracked, drifting further apart each night. The remaining question was a yes-or-no.

