A thirsty Crow had been searching all afternoon for water and was nearly ready to give up. This was by the beach.

Caw the crow, dry-throated and desperate, alighted on the lip of a cool jar half-hidden in shadow. The water inside sat at 5 centimeters from the bottom — too deep for her beak. Around the base lay a scatter of small marbles, and she began to drop them in one by one. She counted: 10 marbles in all. With each soft plink, the surface climbed a careful 1 centimeter higher.

Question: the new water level in the jar (in centimeters) after all 10 marbles have been dropped in?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
I multiply the number of marbles by the rise per marble and add the starting level.

{"tool_calls":[{"name":"eval","args":{"form":"(let [rise-per-stone 1 start-cm 5 n-stones 10] (+ start-cm (* n-stones rise-per-stone)))"}}]}
<|end|>


