The Hare and the Tortoise had argued for as long as anyone could remember about who was truly the faster. All this took place by the beach.

12 miles ahead of Mossback, Whisker came upon a small crowd of forest animals who had gathered to watch. He could not resist a chance to boast, and stayed to tell the story of his victory before it was even won. The telling was so long that he dozed off mid-sentence on a tree stump. Meanwhile Mossback kept up a quiet 4-miles-per-hour pace for 5 hours.

Question: who is in the lead by the time Whisker wakes up?
