There was once a band of Bulls so unified that they made the great Lion uneasy. It happened near the garden.

In a valley grassland threaded by a slow stream, 6 bulls that had once watered together now drank at separate bends. Roar the lion moved through the reeds without complaint, never pressing, never showing more than a flick of tail. From the heron-haunted bank, he watched Gale wade in alone, far from the others. He counted on 1 day per bull to do the work properly — no rushing, no warning bellows carrying across the water. Roar sat back to total what those days, multiplied across the broken herd, would come to.

Question: how many total days Roar will need to defeat all 6 bulls?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
{"tool_calls":[{"name":"eval","args":{"form":"(let [bulls 6 days-per-bull 1] (* bulls days-per-bull))"}}]}
<|end|>


