The Lion stalked the field where the Bulls had grazed in peace for many seasons.

Along an old fence-line that the herd had once walked together each evening, 4 bulls now drifted past the rails singly. Every bull had a measured strength of 11, and Mane the lion, at 12, padded the far side untroubled by what others thought. One bull at the fence was no contest for her; the herd at full muster, however, mounted a combined strength of 44, which would have flung the lion clean off the rails. The bulls' unease left them wide-eyed with fear, drifting further apart each night. The remaining question was a yes-or-no.

Question: whether Mane can defeat each bull alone (lion-strength > bull-strength) yet would lose against the herd combined (lion-strength < combined-strength)?
