By the end of the season, the village had a saying about Tom on the hill. The young shepherd had given the alarm without cause 3 times, and on each of those days 7 villagers had hurried out to help — a round trip that took 6 minutes each. They counted the cost of trust, slowly, and determined the time had not been spent well.

Write a Clojure expression that computes how many total minutes the villagers spent answering the 3 false alarms.
