In a wide clearing rimmed by tall grass, 4 bulls stood at suspicious distances, each of strength 10. Roar the lion crossed the clearing untroubled by what others thought, knowing his own strength to be 11. Single-handedly against a single bull, the lion held the upper paw; but if the herd closed ranks the combined strength of 40 would have made short work of him. The lion sat in the long shadow at the edge and considered: did victory depend strictly on keeping them apart?

