Once a Country Mouse invited her City cousin to dine at her humble home.

On a flat stone in a meadow clearing, Whisk placed a woven basket holding 6 hazelnuts, gathered under the autumn trees. 3 mice had come for the feast — Nibble among them, eyeing the basket his thoughts already on more and remembering richer fare. Yet the country mouse insisted the meal be divided fairly, whole nuts only, with whatever leftover was set aside for the squirrels. The share each mouse received was the same.

Write a Clojure expression that computes how many whole pieces of food each mouse receives if any leftover is set aside.
