It is hard to be believed twice when you have lied even once — a lesson every shepherd must one day learn.

Each Saturday the village reeve walked up to the meadow and reviewed the week's alarms. The custom long ago set the limit at 4 false alarms; beyond that, the village considered itself excused from coming. Tom's tally for the week stood at 6 false alarms when the reeve opened his ledger.

Question: whether the villagers will come on the next alarm (return the string "yes" or "no")?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
I compare alarms-so-far against the threshold and return 'yes' if below, 'no' otherwise.

{"tool_calls":[{"name":"eval","args":{"form":"(let [threshold 4 alarms-so-far 6] (if (< alarms-so-far threshold) \"yes\" \"no\"))"}}]}
<|end|>


