In the farm the rumor went that Charlie's goose laid silver as well as golden eggs, but he only smiled and said nothing of the kind. The goose laid 2 golden eggs a day, and at the market each egg fetched 40 coins. After 15 days of steady laying, every morning he would carry the eggs to the market folded inside a cloth, with a hungry gleam in his eye at the soft weight against his hip, listening to the coins jingle home each evening.

Question: how many coins Charlie had earned in all from the goose's eggs?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Let me compute that.

{"tool_calls":[{"name":"eval","args":{"form":"(let [per-day 2 days 15 per-egg-coins 40 total-eggs (* per-day days)] (* total-eggs per-egg-coins))"}}]}
<|end|>


