Greed has cost more than one creature what they already had.

Rex the dog arrived at Charlie's back gate with 5 bones stacked carefully in a small basket. Charlie eyed the pile and offered a deal: hand over 4 bones of those plain bones, and he would give back the same number of much bigger ones from a sack in the shed. He agreed, his eyes greedy with want. But when Charlie returned, only 3 bones dropped from the sack into the basket — fewer than promised, and Charlie shrugged as if he ought to be grateful.

Question: how many bones Rex has after the trade?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
{"tool_calls":[{"name":"eval","args":{"form":"(let [start-bones 5 bones-given 4 bones-received 3] (+ (- start-bones bones-given) bones-received))"}}]}
<|end|>


