At dusk, the boy's grandfather walked up to the meadow and helped count the flock. There had been 76 sheep that morning. A wolf had come at midday, and Tom had shouted for help — in a panic, but no help came. The grandfather, wishing she had been more careful, walked the line of the flock and found 15 sheep were missing, scattered to the gullies and the woods.

