In the heart of an open meadow stood 5 bulls, each tested at the spring tournament to be of strength 8. Roar the lion watched from the long grass untroubled by what others thought, his own measured strength known to be 15. Bull by bull, he could outmatch any one of them one-on-one. But when the bulls had stood shoulder to shoulder, their unified strength came to 40 — too great for any single lion. The question now was simply whether the lion's only winning path lay through dividing the herd.

