Among the small folk of the meadow, no two neighbors lived more differently than the Ant and the Grasshopper.

"Why bother?" sang the Grasshopper one bright noon, lounging at the lip of Toc's burrow. Toc did not stop, only set another grain into the bag with the small satisfaction of one pleased with her small fortune. "Because winter," she said simply. And so it was that Toc worked the whole 56 days of summer and finished with 280 grains stored away — even as the Grasshopper laughed and chirped the long afternoons away.

