Rex the dog trotted across a low stone footbridge with 6 bones clamped firmly between his jaws, feeling very pleased with the morning's prize. Halfway over, he glanced down at the slow brown water and saw — with a hungry gleam in his eye — what looked like another dog below, with the very same load. He opened his mouth to snatch at that other dog's bone, but of course the moment his jaws parted a single bone tumbled away into the stream and was gone. He stood blinking, wishing she had been more careful.

