"Why bother?" sang the Grasshopper one bright noon, lounging at the lip of Bit's burrow. Bit did not stop, only set another seed into the hole with the small satisfaction of one pleased with her small fortune. "Because winter," they said simply. And so it was that by the close of summer Bit had gathered 272 seeds in all, carrying 8 seeds home each day — even as the Grasshopper laughed and chirped the long afternoons away.

Write a Clojure expression that computes how many days Bit spent at the gathering.
