The Hare loved nothing better than the sound of his own boasts; the Tortoise, nothing better than a long quiet walk.

The badger judge tracked the race from a low knoll. Hopper kept up an unbroken 6 miles per hour, with a smug grin, and Mossback held a steady 1 mile per hour, stepping deliberately. The badger looked up from his sundial when the gap between them reached exactly 30 miles. Knowing both paces, he sat down to figure how many hours had passed since the start.

Write a Clojure expression that computes how many whole hours they had been running.
