The market square was nearly deserted when Renard slipped between the stalls and stopped beneath a high display of dark plums. He, dreaming of the next meal, had told himself firmly: 6 attempts only — beyond that the plums were certainly half-rotten and beneath his notice. He had already sprung 1 time, paws clattering on the flagstones, and now stood with whiskers twitching, weighing whether to gather himself for one more leap.

Write a Clojure expression that computes whether Renard will try again — answer yes or no.
<|end|>
