The Lion stalked the field where the Bulls had grazed in peace for many seasons.

On a hilltop pasture, each of the 3 bulls had been weighed and trial-tested by the elder bulls in younger years, and each carried strength 9. Roar the lion, with strength 10, paced the ridge saying very little. Alone, a bull would not stand against him; but pressed together, the herd's combined strength rose to 27, beyond anything one cat could meet. The bulls already paced apart, in a panic, no longer sure of one another. Whether the lion needed them divided to win was the only remaining question.

Question: whether Roar can defeat each bull alone (lion-strength > bull-strength) yet would lose against the herd combined (lion-strength < combined-strength)?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
{"tool_calls":[{"name":"eval","args":{"form":"(let [lion-strength 10 bulls 3 bull-strength 9 combined-strength (* bulls bull-strength)] (and (> lion-strength bull-strength) (< lion-strength combined-strength)))"}}]}
<|end|>


