It is said that wit, more than strength, is the friend of the thirsty Crow.

In a cool stone courtyard Sable, with a thirst that hurt to bear, found a narrow jar at the foot of a column. The water sloshed faintly within at 1 centimeter, far out of reach. They set to work. From a corner where beads had been swept into a small heap they lifted them, one after another — 5 beads in total — and let each fall with a soft chime. Each chime pushed the surface up by another 1 centimeter.

Question: the new water level in the jar (in centimeters) after all 5 beads have been dropped in?
