A small crowd had gathered at the half-way ridge to watch. Whisker, with great whoops of laughter, ran past at 9 miles per hour, and Slowpoke plodded along with eyes always on the path at 3 miles per hour. By the time the sun had moved a fair way across the sky, the lead had grown to 18 miles between them. From the two speeds and the present gap, the spectators wanted to reconstruct how long the race had been running.

Question: how many whole hours they had been running?
<|end|>
