It is the way of the Ant to gather, and the way of the Grasshopper to play.

Halfway through summer, Tic stood with a smug grin beside a jar that was already heavier than he could easily drag. Each acorn had been chosen, weighed in two feelers, and tucked carefully in. The Grasshopper passed by humming a tune and laughed at the trouble Tic took over so small a thing. He only kept on; by the close of summer Tic had gathered 144 acorns in all, carrying 6 acorns home each day.

Question: how many days Tic spent at the gathering?
