On the eve of the first spring thaw — at the end of 35 days of winter — the two neighbors sat very differently. In a bag at the heart of the burrow, Toc had begun winter with 155 nuts, and across the cold weeks she had taken only 2 nuts a day. Chirp, in his thin basket, had begun with only 7 nuts, and ate 1 nut per day, dreaming of the next meal. A stockpile, once it runs out, cannot go below zero.

