Bell the dog had set out that morning meaning to bring home 9 bones for her secret corner under the rose bush. Crossing the stream on the way back, she saw her reflection — imagining all that he might gain — and snatched at the shadow's bone. One bone spun away into the current, and she arrived home with one fewer than the count she had been so proud of. She sat by the rose bush, wondering how it had come to this, comparing what she meant to have brought against what was actually in the pile.

