Two creatures of the meadow approached the coming winter very differently.

At the beach, Bit the ant bent low over the warm earth, collecting one grain at a time and lining the bag that sat half-buried by the burrow's mouth. While the Grasshopper fiddled in the long grass nearby, Bit worked content in her quiet life, knowing the cold months would come whether or not anyone sang for them. So Bit worked the whole 43 days of summer and finished with 258 grains stored away.

Write a Clojure expression that computes how many grains Bit carried home each day.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
{"tool_calls":[{"name":"eval","args":{"form":"(let [total 258 days 43] (quot total days))"}}]}
<|end|>


