The badger judge tracked the race from a low knoll. Hopper kept up an unbroken 5 miles per hour, swaggering through the underbrush, and Shelly held a steady 2 miles per hour, with eyes always on the path. The badger looked up from his sundial when the gap between them reached exactly 9 miles. Knowing both paces, he sat down to figure how many hours had passed since the start.

Write a Clojure expression that computes how many whole hours they had been running.
