It is the way of the Ant to gather, and the way of the Grasshopper to play.

"Why bother?" sang the Grasshopper one bright noon, lounging at the lip of Bit's burrow. Bit did not stop, only set another acorn into the pouch with the small satisfaction of one content in her quiet life. "Because winter," they said simply. And so it was that by the close of summer Bit had gathered 396 acorns in all, carrying 6 acorns home each day — even as the Grasshopper laughed and chirped the long afternoons away.

Question: how many days Bit spent at the gathering?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Time to write the form.

{"tool_calls":[{"name":"eval","args":{"form":"(let [total 396 per-day 6] (quot total per-day))"}}]}
<|end|>


