A small crowd had gathered at the half-way ridge to watch. Whisker, puffed up with pride, ran past at 4 miles per hour, and Shelly plodded along stepping deliberately at 2 miles per hour. By the time the sun had moved a fair way across the sky, the lead had grown to 4 miles between them. From the two speeds and the present gap, the spectators wanted to reconstruct how long the race had been running.

