A Dog was crossing a stream with a fine bone in his mouth, and was very pleased with himself.

Rex the dog trotted across a low stone footbridge with 7 bones clamped firmly between his jaws, feeling very pleased with the morning's prize. Halfway over, he glanced down at the slow brown water and saw — his thoughts already on more — what looked like another dog below, with the very same load. He opened his mouth to snatch at that other dog's bone, but of course the moment his jaws parted a single bone tumbled away into the stream and was gone. He stood blinking, wishing she had been more careful.

