Three Bulls had grazed and fought together for so long that no Lion dared trouble them.

Along an old fence-line that the herd had once walked together each evening, 3 bulls now drifted past the rails singly. Every bull had a measured strength of 10, and Roar the lion, at 14, padded the far side stepping deliberately. One bull at the fence was no contest for him; the herd at full muster, however, mounted a combined strength of 30, which would have flung the lion clean off the rails. The bulls' unease left them wide-eyed with fear, drifting further apart each night. The remaining question was a yes-or-no.

