Rex the dog arrived at Beatrice's back gate with 14 bones stacked carefully in a small basket. Beatrice eyed the pile and offered a deal: hand over 8 bones of those plain bones, and she would give back the same number of much bigger ones from a sack in the shed. He agreed, with a hungry gleam in his eye. But when Beatrice returned, only 7 bones dropped from the sack into the basket — fewer than promised, and Beatrice shrugged as if he ought to be grateful.

Write a Clojure expression that computes how many bones Rex has after the trade.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
I subtract what was given away from the start, then add back what was received.

{"tool_calls":[{"name":"eval","args":{"form":"(let [start-bones 14 bones-given 8 bones-received 7] (+ (- start-bones bones-given) bones-received))"}}]}
<|end|>


