Every shepherd in the valley knew the danger of crying wolf for sport.

The flock that morning held 40 sheep. When a wolf came down from the ridge, Jess ran to the village edge calling for help, with growing alarm, but the doors stayed shut. By the time the old shepherd at the far end of the village heard the noise and walked up, the wolf was gone and 8 sheep had vanished into the gullies — too far now to gather back.

Question: how many sheep Jess has left in the flock?
