All summer long, the Ant worked while the Grasshopper sang.

Midway through a winter that ran 61 days from end to end, two ledgers told two stories. Tic the ant had begun with 87 crumbs stored snugly in the bag at the back of the burrow, and ate exactly 1 crumb per day. Hum the grasshopper had begun with only 13 crumbs in their thin pouch, and they too went through 3 crumbs per day, her hands trembling. Whichever stockpile emptied first, the count would simply rest at zero.

Question: how many crumbs Tic has left at the end of winter?
