There was once a Milkmaid whose dreams ran ahead of her pail.

Carrying a willow basket of duck eggs from the henhouse to the kitchen door, Margery let her thoughts run further than her feet. His thoughts already on more, she traced out the chain on her fingers. The coins from the morning's eggs would buy 5 eggs more; each would warm and hatch under a good broody hen; each grown hen would give 122 eggs a year; and at market each of those would sell for 1 coin. The basket creaked. She did not feel its weight at all.

