In a valley grassland threaded by a slow stream, 4 bulls that had once watered together now drank at separate bends. Mane the lion moved through the reeds stepping deliberately, never pressing, never showing more than a flick of tail. From the heron-haunted bank, she watched Gale wade in alone, far from the others. She counted on 1 day per bull to do the work properly — no rushing, no warning bellows carrying across the water. Mane sat back to total what those days, multiplied across the broken herd, would come to.

Question: how many total days Mane will need to defeat all 4 bulls?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
