A young farmhand at the barn kept a chalk tally on a beam in the barn — one mark for each egg the goose laid, one cross for each coin paid at the market. The goose laid 2 golden eggs a day for 9 days, and when the eggs were finally carried in their basket to the market they fetched 360 coins in all — the boy stood and stared up at the marks, while Robin sat by the door of the barn, happy with what she had, listening to the goose ruffle her feathers.

Write a Clojure expression that computes the price in coins at which each single egg had sold.
