Three Bulls had grazed and fought together for so long that no Lion dared trouble them.

Along an old fence-line that the herd had once walked together each evening, 5 bulls now drifted past the rails singly. Every bull had a measured strength of 6, and Roar the lion, at 7, padded the far side stepping deliberately. One bull at the fence was no contest for him; the herd at full muster, however, mounted a combined strength of 30, which would have flung the lion clean off the rails. The bulls' unease left them her hands trembling, drifting further apart each night. The remaining question was a yes-or-no.

Question: whether Roar can defeat each bull alone (lion-strength > bull-strength) yet would lose against the herd combined (lion-strength < combined-strength)?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
{"tool_calls":[{"name":"eval","args":{"form":"(let [lion-strength 7 bulls 5 bull-strength 6 combined-strength (* bulls bull-strength)] (and (> lion-strength bull-strength) (< lion-strength combined-strength)))"}}]}
<|end|>


