Bess loaded her small cart with the day's milk and set off down the lane to market, the cow's price of 177 coins still heavy on her mind. The cow gave 6 cups a day; at the village square each cup sold steadily for 2 coins. His mouth watering at the thought of more, she did the sum on her fingers as the cart creaked, working out how many such trips she would need before the debt was clear.

