In that part of the forest, no one ever expected the Tortoise to outrun the Hare — yet today the question would be settled.

A curious old badger met Slowpoke on the path and asked how the race was going. "The course is 15 miles," said Slowpoke with eyes always on the path, "and I have walked 14 miles so far." Behind him, Whisker could just be made out, as if the race were already won but lulled by the gentle wind, lounging by a stump. Slowpoke added that he kept a steady 3 miles per hour and meant to finish before sundown.

