The Hare and the Tortoise had argued for as long as anyone could remember about who was truly the faster. This was in the woods.

A traveller passing through stopped to ask about the morning's race. He was told that Mossback, without complaint, had walked a steady 3 miles per hour for 3 hours, and that Hopper, as if the race were already won, had finished 3 miles ahead. "And how fast was the Hare?" he asked, but no one had clocked Hopper directly — only the math could supply the answer.

Write a Clojure expression that computes Hopper's speed in miles per hour.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Hopper's total distance equals the lead plus Mossback's distance; speed equals that total divided by hours.

{"tool_calls":[{"name":"eval","args":{"form":"(let [tortoise-speed 3 hours 3 miles-ahead 3 tortoise-distance (* tortoise-speed hours) hare-distance (+ miles-ahead tortoise-distance)] (quot hare-distance hours))"}}]}
<|end|>


