Along an old fence-line that the herd had once walked together each evening, 3 bulls now drifted past the rails singly. Every bull had a measured strength of 11, and Mane the lion, at 11, padded the far side without complaint. One bull at the fence was no contest for her; the herd at full muster, however, mounted a combined strength of 33, which would have flung the lion clean off the rails. The bulls' unease left them in a panic, drifting further apart each night. The remaining question was a yes-or-no.

