There was once an extraordinary goose whose every morning gift was a single egg of pure gold.

Frank kept a leather-bound diary by the lamp on the kitchen table, and each evening would write down the day's yield from Quill the goose in his careful hand. Over 6 days, the count came out — day after day — as 3, 1, 4, 1, 4, 1. Some mornings the goose laid more than he expected, and Frank would linger in the barn, his thoughts already on more at the warm gold; other days only one or two, and he simply nodded and closed the door.

Write a Clojure expression that computes how many eggs in total were laid over those days.
<|end|>
