Every shepherd in the valley knew the danger of crying wolf for sport.

On market days the villagers gathered to trade, and Jess, watching the flock from a high stone, learned that a single shout would empty the market square. So she shouted — falsely — 4 times. On each occasion, 4 of the busiest villagers ran out from their stalls to help, with growing alarm, and the round trip back cost each of them 17 minutes.

Question: how many total minutes the villagers spent answering the 4 false alarms?
