Carrying a willow basket of duck eggs from the henhouse to the kitchen door, Clara let her thoughts run further than her feet. His mouth watering at the thought of more, she traced out the chain on her fingers. The coins from the morning's eggs would buy 4 eggs more; each would warm and hatch under a good broody hen; each grown hen would give 185 eggs a year; and at market each of those would sell for 5 coins. The basket creaked. She did not feel its weight at all.

Write a Clojure expression that computes how many coins Clara would earn after one year if everything went perfectly.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
{"tool_calls":[{"name":"eval","args":{"form":"(let [eggs 4 eggs-per-hen 185 coins-per-egg 5] (* eggs eggs-per-hen coins-per-egg))"}}]}
<|end|>


