A new shepherd, recently come to the village, asked aloud how many warnings the neighbours would tolerate before they stopped answering at all. The reeve answered honestly: the limit was 5 false alarms. Tom's recent record stood at 4 false alarms, and the new shepherd worked out, by simple comparison, whether help would come the next time.

