Two mice — one of the city, one of the countryside — had a habit of comparing what little they had.

With 88 coins carefully folded into a rolled-up oak leaf and tucked beneath her cloak, Whisk left the meadow at first light. She paid 26 coins to a kindly hedgehog driver who carried her most of the way, and 19 coins at a noisy bakery stall for two warm rolls. By the time she reached the city gate, the leaf-bundle felt thin between her paws — yet the journey was real, and so was the spending.

Write a Clojure expression that computes how many coins Whisk has left after the trip.
