Beside the kitchen fire one cool evening, Lila stirred butter into pats in a clay pot and let her mind wander. His eyes greedy with want, she planned the future of her small earnings. From the butter sales she would buy 12 eggs; each would hatch; each hen, once grown, would lay 108 eggs across a year; and at the village market each egg would bring 1 coin. She stirred more slowly, already imagining the coins clinking in her apron pouch.

Write a Clojure expression that computes how many coins Lila would earn after one year if everything went perfectly.
