Two creatures of the meadow approached the coming winter very differently.

Midway through a winter that ran 54 days from end to end, two ledgers told two stories. Toc the ant had begun with 198 seeds stored snugly in the jar at the back of the burrow, and ate exactly 3 seeds per day. Chirp the grasshopper had begun with only 1 seed in his thin pouch, and he too went through 2 seeds per day, shouting until her voice cracked. Whichever stockpile emptied first, the count would simply rest at zero.

Question: how many seeds Toc has left at the end of winter?
