It is told that many an animal has stood beneath fruit it could not reach and walked away calling it sour.

Along the white stone wall that ringed an old vineyard, a fig tree had grown over the top and dropped its fruit on the wrong side. The lowest dark fig hung 4 feet above the dusty lane where Vix the fox now stood, regretting every careless step that the climb up the slope had cost her so much breath for so little gain. She sprang once to test herself: the bound carried her 2 feet aloft. She settled to count how many such efforts, each lifting 2 feet, would suffice.

Write a Clojure expression that computes the smallest number of leaps Vix needs to reach the fruit.
