For many seasons, 4 bulls had stood shoulder to shoulder in an open meadow, and no predator had dared approach. Then a quarrel split them, and they wandered separately into the long grass. Roar the lion watched from a fold in the land with eyes always on the path, knowing each bull on its own was no longer the same problem as the herd together. He reckoned that, hunting alone, he would need a careful 1 day of stalking and waiting for every single bull. Roar settled in to count the days the whole undertaking would cost.

Question: how many total days Roar will need to defeat all 4 bulls?
