Along an old fence-line that the herd had once walked together each evening, 4 bulls now drifted past the rails singly. Every bull had a measured strength of 3, and Roar the lion, at 14, padded the far side untroubled by what others thought. One bull at the fence was no contest for him; the herd at full muster, however, mounted a combined strength of 12, which would have flung the lion clean off the rails. The bulls' unease left them shouting until her voice cracked, drifting further apart each night. The remaining question was a yes-or-no.

