Edward kept Quill the goose on a quiet farm at the edge of the village. Every morning, without fail, the goose laid 3 golden eggs in the same straw nest. He would lift each egg with both hands, happy with what she had, and place it in a wooden basket beside the door. The ritual went on for 20 days — sun, wind, or rain — and Edward began to wonder how many golden eggs had passed through his hands by the end of that long stretch.

Write a Clojure expression that computes how many eggs the goose laid in total over those 20 days.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
I multiply the eggs per day by the number of days.

{"tool_calls":[{"name":"eval","args":{"form":"(let [per-day 3 days 20] (* per-day days))"}}]}
<|end|>


