A hungry Fox came upon a vine of grapes hanging just out of reach.

Beneath a low vine in an old vineyard Vix the fox had been leaping at a heavy cluster of ripe purple grapes for the better part of an hour. She, weak with hunger, had resolved before starting that 4 attempts would be her limit — beyond that, she would call the grapes sour and walk away. So far she had sprung 6 times, paws scrabbling at the leaves, and now she stood panting in the dust to weigh whether the next jump was worth its breath.

Question: whether Vix will try again — answer yes or no?
