On a hilltop pasture, each of the 5 bulls had been weighed and trial-tested by the elder bulls in younger years, and each carried strength 7. Mane the lion, with strength 7, paced the ridge untroubled by what others thought. Alone, a bull would not stand against her; but pressed together, the herd's combined strength rose to 35, beyond anything one cat could meet. The bulls already paced apart, in a panic, no longer sure of one another. Whether the lion needed them divided to win was the only remaining question.

