What the Dog thought he saw beneath the water turned out to be his own reflection.

Bell the dog had collected 5 sticks by the riverbank when Charlie came along leading a small handcart. He offered her a trade: 4 sticks of those green sticks for the same number of seasoned hardwood pieces from the cart, which (so he swore) burned twice as long. She pushed the sticks over, his eyes greedy with want. From the cart Charlie drew only 3 sticks and rolled the cart away whistling.

