Greed and patience, as everyone knows, do not sit at the same table — and a golden-egg goose tests them both.

The village tax collector wanted to know the goose's typical yield, and would not be put off by talk of varying days. Alex laid out the 3 days' counts on a slate — 1, 3, 2 — and set to working out the rounded-down average, his heart sinking of the day they had ever mentioned the bird in the village square.

Question: the average eggs per day, rounded down to a whole number?
