In that part of the forest, no one ever expected the Tortoise to outrun the Hare — yet today the question would be settled. It happened atop the hilltop.

A farmer leaning on his fence watched the racers go past. Bramble flew by boasting at every turn at 6 miles per hour; Mossback came behind at a calm 2 miles per hour, untroubled by what others thought. Some while later the farmer wandered down the road and found Bramble a clear 8 miles ahead of Mossback. He scratched his beard and tried to work out how long they had been running.

Question: how many whole hours they had been running?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The gap grows by (hare-speed minus tortoise-speed) each hour, so I divide miles-ahead by that gap rate.

{"tool_calls":[{"name":"eval","args":{"form":"(let [hare-speed 6 tortoise-speed 2 miles-ahead 8 gap-per-hour (- hare-speed tortoise-speed)] (quot miles-ahead gap-per-hour))"}}]}
<|end|>


