There was once an extraordinary goose whose every morning gift was a single egg of pure gold.

More than once Bob had heard a sly voice whisper that the goose was wasted on slow daily laying. But he swallowed the thought each time, fed the bird, and let the gold come at its own pace. The goose laid 1 golden egg a day, and at the market each egg fetched 31 coins. By the time the small chest of coins beside the hearth held 868 coins in all, he sat by the hearth, pleased with her small fortune, and looked at the worn ledger where every egg, every coin, every trip to the market had been written down in a careful hand.

Question: for how many days the goose had been laying?
