A young farmhand at the village liked to come round at sunrise just to watch Sam collect from the goose. The bird would settle, ruffle, and stand, leaving 3 golden eggs in the straw — never more, never fewer. Sam would gather them happy with what she had, smiling at the boy, and tuck them into a folded cloth. They kept up the routine for 17 days, and at the end the boy asked, eyes wide, just how many golden eggs the goose had given altogether.

