The small folk of the meadow whispered, on the longest night, about how the two neighbors were faring. Winter, all said, would last 45 days in all. Toc the ant, content in her quiet life, had laid in 239 grains in the hole at the back of the burrow and ate only 1 grain a day. Skip the grasshopper had managed only 26 grains in her bag, and ate 3 grains a day, regretting every careless step. Neither stockpile could carry a count below zero.

Write a Clojure expression that computes how many grains Toc has left at the end of winter.
