It is the way of the Ant to gather, and the way of the Grasshopper to play.

Midway through a winter that ran 79 days from end to end, two ledgers told two stories. Tic the ant had begun with 94 seeds stored snugly in the bag at the back of the burrow, and ate exactly 2 seeds per day. Hum the grasshopper had begun with only 19 seeds in their thin jar, and they too went through 2 seeds per day, wide-eyed with fear. Whichever stockpile emptied first, the count would simply rest at zero.

Write a Clojure expression that computes how many seeds Tic has left at the end of winter.
