Rex the dog had set out that morning meaning to bring home 5 bones for his secret corner under the rose bush. Crossing the stream on the way back, he saw his reflection — his thoughts already on more — and snatched at the shadow's bone. One bone spun away into the current, and he arrived home with one fewer than the count he had been so proud of. He sat by the rose bush, wondering how it had come to this, comparing what he meant to have brought against what was actually in the pile.

Write a Clojure expression that computes how many bones Rex fell short by, compared to what he expected to bring home.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
{"tool_calls":[{"name":"eval","args":{"form":"(let [expected-bones 5 actual-bones (dec expected-bones)] (- expected-bones actual-bones))"}}]}
<|end|>


