There was once a band of Bulls so unified that they made the great Lion uneasy. All this took place on the beach.

In the heart of an open meadow stood 3 bulls, each tested at the spring tournament to be of strength 3. Mane the lion watched from the long grass stepping deliberately, her own measured strength known to be 8. Bull by bull, she could outmatch any one of them one-on-one. But when the bulls had stood shoulder to shoulder, their unified strength came to 9 — too great for any single lion. The question now was simply whether the lion's only winning path lay through dividing the herd.

Write a Clojure expression that computes whether Mane can defeat each bull alone (lion-strength > bull-strength) yet would lose against the herd combined (lion-strength < combined-strength).
