More than once Emily had heard a sly voice whisper that the goose was wasted on slow daily laying. But she swallowed the thought each time, fed the bird, and let the gold come at its own pace. The goose laid 2 golden eggs a day, and at the market each egg fetched 45 coins. By the time the small chest of coins beside the hearth held 900 coins in all, she sat by the hearth, content in her quiet life, and looked at the worn ledger where every egg, every coin, every trip to the market had been written down in a careful hand.

Write a Clojure expression that computes for how many days the goose had been laying.
<|end|>
