In a wide clearing rimmed by tall grass, 4 bulls stood at suspicious distances, each of strength 9. Roar the lion crossed the clearing without complaint, knowing his own strength to be 11. Single-handedly against a single bull, the lion held the upper paw; but if the herd closed ranks the combined strength of 36 would have made short work of him. The lion sat in the long shadow at the edge and considered: did victory depend strictly on keeping them apart?

Question: whether Roar can defeat each bull alone (lion-strength > bull-strength) yet would lose against the herd combined (lion-strength < combined-strength)?
