Strength shared is strength multiplied — a truth the Lion knew well, and worked patiently to undo. This was near the beach.

At the center of a wide clearing rimmed in shoulder-high grass, 3 bulls had been grazing in a loose, suspicious ring — no longer a single mass. Roar the lion circled the perimeter with eyes always on the path, the grass swallowing every footfall. From a tussock, he watched a young bull turn its back and wander deeper into the green. The lion knew from long practice that solitary prey meant 3 days of patient work for each kill. As wide-eyed with fear bellows sometimes drifted through the clearing at dusk, Roar sat down to tally what the whole campaign would cost in days.

