Midway through a winter that ran 53 days from end to end, two ledgers told two stories. Toc the ant had begun with 161 acorns stored snugly in the hole at the back of the burrow, and ate exactly 1 acorn per day. Skip the grasshopper had begun with only 1 acorn in her thin pouch, and she too went through 1 acorn per day, shouting until her voice cracked. Whichever stockpile emptied first, the count would simply rest at zero.

