On a chipped saucer in the corner of a damp city cellar, Whisk arranged 8 butter pats freshly stolen from a dairy. 2 mice sat around the saucer in flickering candlelight, including the country guest. Whisk, his eyes greedy with want, fretted over the arrangement; Nibble simply waited, happy with what she had, ready to accept whichever share fell out of an honest split. Whole pats each, leftover set aside.

Question: how many whole pieces of food each mouse receives if any leftover is set aside?
