Strength shared is strength multiplied — a truth the Lion knew well, and worked patiently to undo. It happened at the edge of the garden.

On a wide hilltop pasture, 3 bulls had been grazing under the morning sun until petty rivalries pulled them apart. Thorn moved north of the spring, Boulder south, and the rest scattered to lower slopes. Mane the lion crouched among the scrub at the ridge without complaint, taking the long view. She had learned, after one bruising failure, that a single bull on open ground took her a measured 3 days to bring down. With the herd now broken, Mane began to figure how many days the entire hunt would consume.

Question: how many total days Mane will need to defeat all 3 bulls?
