The Hare loved nothing better than the sound of his own boasts; the Tortoise, nothing better than a long quiet walk.

A curious old badger met Shelly on the path and asked how the race was going. "The course is 24 miles," said Shelly without complaint, "and I have walked 2 miles so far." Behind him, Pip could just be made out, boasting at every turn but with legs heavy from sprinting, lounging by a stump. Shelly added that she kept a steady 3 miles per hour and meant to finish before sundown.

