All summer long, the Ant worked while the Grasshopper sang.

That year the cold months stretched 52 days from first snow to last frost. Bit kept a careful tally: 71 acorns in the jar by the wall at the start, and they drew 1 acorn from it every morning, puffed up with pride of their planning. Chirp, hidden in the dry stalks, had begun the winter with only 27 acorns in his pouch, and chewed through 1 acorn a day. The count, of course, cannot go below zero for either of them.

