Winter had come at last to the meadow, and lasted 86 days from first frost to first thaw. In Bit the ant's neat bag sat 212 seeds, gathered in the bright weeks of summer; Bit ate 1 seed each day, no more, content in her quiet life. In Hum the grasshopper's thin jar sat only 21 seeds, and they too ate 1 seed a day, wishing she had been more careful. If a stockpile runs out, the count cannot go below zero.

Write a Clojure expression that computes how many seeds Bit has left at the end of winter.
