Midway through a winter that ran 51 days from end to end, two ledgers told two stories. Bit the ant had begun with 139 acorns stored snugly in the hole at the back of the burrow, and ate exactly 2 acorns per day. Hum the grasshopper had begun with only 17 acorns in their thin bag, and they too went through 1 acorn per day, her hands trembling. Whichever stockpile emptied first, the count would simply rest at zero.

Write a Clojure expression that computes how many acorns Bit has left at the end of winter.
