The village tax collector wanted to know the goose's typical yield, and would not be put off by talk of varying days. Beatrice laid out the 5 days' counts on a slate — 5, 4, 5, 6, 5 — and set to working out the rounded-down average, regretting every careless step of the day she had ever mentioned the bird in the village square.

