Strength shared is strength multiplied — a truth the Lion knew well, and worked patiently to undo.

In a wide clearing rimmed by tall grass, 5 bulls stood at suspicious distances, each of strength 4. Mane the lion crossed the clearing untroubled by what others thought, knowing her own strength to be 14. Single-handedly against a single bull, the lion held the upper paw; but if the herd closed ranks the combined strength of 20 would have made short work of her. The lion sat in the long shadow at the edge and considered: did victory depend strictly on keeping them apart?

