In the heart of an open meadow stood 3 bulls, each tested at the spring tournament to be of strength 9. Roar the lion watched from the long grass with eyes always on the path, his own measured strength known to be 10. Bull by bull, he could outmatch any one of them one-on-one. But when the bulls had stood shoulder to shoulder, their unified strength came to 27 — too great for any single lion. The question now was simply whether the lion's only winning path lay through dividing the herd.

Write a Clojure expression that computes whether Roar can defeat each bull alone (lion-strength > bull-strength) yet would lose against the herd combined (lion-strength < combined-strength).
<|end|>
<|asst|>
{"tool_calls":[{"name":"eval","args":{"form":"(let [lion-strength 10 bulls 3 bull-strength 9 combined-strength (* bulls bull-strength)] (and (> lion-strength bull-strength) (< lion-strength combined-strength)))"}}]}
<|end|>


