Margery had spent 185 coins on a fine brown cow, and his mouth watering at the thought of more, she sat down to plan the days ahead. Each morning her wooden pail would fill with 3 cups of warm milk; each cup, taken to market, would fetch 1 coin. She marked a tally on the inside of her cottage door, telling herself she would make a notch every evening until the cow had paid for itself.

