At the edge of the forest, where the trees gave way to a grazing strip, 6 bulls had wandered out one by one rather than as the close-pressed mass they used to be. Roar the lion watched from the deeper shade with steady, careful steps, ears half-folded, tail quiet. He knew the terrain well enough to be certain of his timing — 4 days of stalking and one sudden lunge, no more, no less, for each bull alone. With the herd's old solidarity in shreds, Roar began to add up how many days of careful hunting lay ahead.

Question: how many total days Roar will need to defeat all 6 bulls?
<|end|>
