Among the small folk of the meadow, no two neighbors lived more differently than the Ant and the Grasshopper.

On the first hard morning of winter — a season that would last 69 days in all — Chirp the grasshopper came scratching at Toc's burrow, dreaming of the next meal. Inside the burrow, Toc sat beside a bag of 254 acorns and ate 2 acorns each day. The Grasshopper had only 21 acorns in a bag, and ate 3 acorns a day. (No stockpile can drop below zero.)

Write a Clojure expression that computes how many acorns Toc has left at the end of winter.
<|end|>
