The Fox crept through the orchard and found himself eyeing a tempting cluster of grapes.

In the corner of an orchard Vix the fox stopped beneath a low arbor where a heavy bunch of purple grapes hung 6 feet above the trodden grass. Vix, his stomach hollow with hunger, paused there with her mouth watering at the dusty bloom on each grape. A trial spring carried her 2 feet into the air, and she reasoned that each leap, if she could somehow build upon the last, would bring the prize 2 feet closer.

