It is said that a meal among friends is sweeter than feasting alone, and easier to count.

In the warm hollow of an old oak, Nibble the country mouse spread a worn pouch open on the moss floor. Inside lay 13 cheese rinds, saved scrap by scrap from a farmer's broken plate. 5 mice had gathered for the meal — including Nibble and Squeak, the city visitor — and they sat in a careful ring, happy with what she had. The host counted out portions slowly, leaving any remainder for the next day's breakfast.

Write a Clojure expression that computes how many whole pieces of food each mouse receives if any leftover is set aside.
