Under a row of elms, Hopper held a steady 4 miles per hour, with a smug grin, while Shelly, stepping deliberately, kept 1 mile per hour without flagging. At one moment a passing finch noted the gap had reached exactly 12 miles. Given those two unwavering paces, the question was simply how long they had been at it.

Question: how many whole hours they had been running?
