In that part of the forest, no one ever expected the Tortoise to outrun the Hare — yet today the question would be settled. It happened in the woods.

Beneath the row of elms that lined the racing path, two very different paces fell into rhythm. Whisker, with great whoops of laughter, sprang ahead at 10 miles per hour. Slowpoke, with steady, careful steps, set down each foot in turn at exactly 1 mile per hour and refused to be hurried. The pact was straightforward: keep those paces for 4 hours, then let the lead speak for itself.

Write a Clojure expression that computes how many miles ahead Whisker is after 4 hours.
<|end|>
