There was once a band of Bulls so unified that they made the great Lion uneasy.

At dusk on a flat plain, the silhouettes of the surviving bulls were spread far across the grass. There had been 5 bulls at the start of the long season, and Mane the lion had taken 3 since then, one by one. The remaining shapes stood in a panic, each in its own patch of fading light. She watched the long shadows lean across the plain with steady, careful steps and counted how many bulls of the original herd were still left to take.

Question: how many bulls remain?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
{"tool_calls":[{"name":"eval","args":{"form":"(let [bulls 5 bulls-defeated 3] (- bulls bulls-defeated))"}}]}
<|end|>


