The boy on the hill thought the trick clever the first time he played it.

By the end of the season, the village had a saying about Lou on the hill. The young shepherd had given the alarm without cause 3 times, and on each of those days 9 villagers had hurried out to help — a round trip that took 7 minutes each. They counted the cost of trust, slowly, and determined the time had not been spent well.

Question: how many total minutes the villagers spent answering the 3 false alarms?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Let me compute that.

